{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"update2.json\", \"summary\": \"Refined the discriminator of investigation 7428c4a1533941c1bcd9707354ba9245-question-0 to state precisely what the retained receipts do and do not cover, so the remaining cell is not re-run needlessly. The cell it still names is a re-synchronisation that discards the origin's entries while the origin's decided index also advances inside that same re-synchronisation; the six retained configurations separate the two features (origin decided index right after the re-synchronisation was 0 wherever the two buffered entries were discarded - cases H, I, J, K and the long-poll case L, which waited 30113 ms and still read 0 - and 3 wherever they were kept, cases M and N), so the discard and the within-re-synchronisation advance have not been observed together. Case L's endpoint does show both features holding later in the run (origin decided values 22,33,34,35, entries 11 and 12 gone, decided index 4, caller's index still shifted to 4 holding entry 35), but that progress arrives after the re-election rather than from the re-synchronisation, so it does not exhibit a placeholder consumed by the re-synchronisation itself. Because the placeholder queue is not readable through the actor's handle - the harness observes only the decided index, the decided suffix and the reported leader - a further case could only reach that cell through the same endpoints and would refine the second mechanism's intermediate step rather than its conclusion. The update cites actor_drain_notifiers, actor_pending_assigned_field and the flush/accept-sync sources behind the condition, changes only source_ids and the discriminator, keeps the question, hypothesis and active disposition, and requests no execution; CLI validation returned valid: true with no diagnostics, and no source, harness or trusted artifact was modified.\"}"}}
